Wave of Darkness now support Steam Controller thanks to the template created by "mUnday"!

Hi all!

Well, we really can't hide smiles from our faces when we saw the thread created by user "mUnday" who announced that Wave of Darkness now supports Steam Controller, all thanks to his incredible effort.

All you have to do is to find the template created by "mUnday" and that's basically it.

Here it is how it works:

[list]
[*]ABXY are mapped for hotbar 1-4, while holding the left grip ABXY switch to 5-8;
[*]Also can toggle through hotbars 1-5 with the right and left shoulder buttons;
[*]Right grip is TAB and will target closest enemy;
[*]Inventory, skills etc are mapped to the directional pad; 
[*]Quest log is mapped to right pad click;
[*]Double "tap" the right pad for quick save;
[*]Start button is ESC and will close windows or go to the Menu; 
[*]Back button opens the map; 
[*]Left click is set for ready weapon (definitely going to change it, maybe to taunt - mUnday);
[*]Right pad is set for mouse;
[*]Right and Left Trigger are left and right mouse click; 
[/list]

Thats it for now! If you have a Steam Controller, check it out and feel free to update and suggest improvements or changes to mUnday in [url=http://steamcommunity.com/app/316370/discussions/0/496881136928392983/]this thread[/url]!

Once again, [b]MASSIVE[/b] thanks mUnday!

